          "short": "Min $=1$, $Q_1=9$, $Q_2=18$, $Q_3=27$, Max $=35$.",
          "worked": "$$M_p=\\frac{13+1}{2}=7$$\nThere are 13 values. The median is the 7th value, $18\\text{.}$ Exclude it when splitting the data into two halves.\n$$\\begin{aligned}Q_1&=\\frac{9+9}{2}=9\\\\Q_2&=18\\\\Q_3&=\\frac{25+29}{2}=27\\end{aligned}$$\nThe minimum is $1$ and the maximum is $35\\text{.}$ Draw the box from $9$ to $27$, its median at $18$, and whiskers to $1$ and $35\\text{.}$",
