        "answer": {
          "short": "Min $=8$, $Q_1=11$, $Q_2=17$, $Q_3=21$, Max $=29$.",
          "worked": "$$M_p=\\frac{14+1}{2}=7.5$$\nThere are 14 values. The median is the mean of the 7th and 8th values. Each half contains seven values, so its median is its 4th value.\n$$\\begin{aligned}Q_1&=11\\\\Q_2&=\\frac{14+20}{2}=17\\\\Q_3&=21\\end{aligned}$$\nThe minimum is $8$ and the maximum is $29$. Draw the box from $11$ to $21$, its median at $17$, and whiskers to $8$ and $29$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p26-q3-b-solution-plot",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"graph\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[{\"name\":\"answerBlue\",\"hex\":\"268CFF\",\"reason\":\"answer box plot\"}],\"reference\":\"page 26, 3b answer plot\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.28cm,y=0.4cm]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\definecolor{answerBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}\n\\path[use as bounding box] (4.3,-1) rectangle (30.7,3.2);\n\\draw[black,dotted,line width=0.15pt,xstep=1,ystep=0.5] (5,0) grid (30,3);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.5pt] (5,0)--(30,0);\n\\foreach \\v in {5,10,15,20,25,30} {\\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (\\v,0)--(\\v,-0.25);\\node[below] at (\\v,-0.25) {\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}$\\v$\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};}\n\\draw[answerBlue,line width=0.8pt] (8,1.5)--(11,1.5) (21,1.5)--(29,1.5) (11,0.7) rectangle (21,2.3);\n\\fill[answerBlue] (16.95,0.7) rectangle (17.05,2.3);\n\\draw[answerBlue,line width=0.4pt] (8,1.2)--(8,1.8) (29,1.2)--(29,1.8);\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
